WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.732 --> 00:00:03.793
Bobbie ran to the kitchen.

2
00:00:04.273 --> 00:00:06.275
"Mother Daddy isn't isn't dead, is he?"

3
00:00:06.295 --> 00:00:10.299
"My darling, no!

4
00:00:10.479 --> 00:00:14.082
What makes you think of something so horrible?"

5
00:00:14.102 --> 00:00:14.643
"I I don't know."

6
00:00:30.572 --> 00:00:33.693
Bobbie didn't mention the clothes she'd seen in her mother's suitcase.

7
00:00:35.533 --> 00:00:36.734
Mother gave her a quick hug.

8
00:00:36.754 --> 00:00:41.295
"Daddy was quite well when I heard from him last," she said.

9
00:00:41.315 --> 00:00:44.296
"And he will come back to us one day.

10
00:00:45.396 --> 00:00:47.177
Don't think such horrible things!"

11
00:00:48.677 --> 00:00:50.458
Later Mother came into the girls' room.

12
00:00:51.678 --> 00:00:53.778
She was going to sleep there, in Phyllis' bed.

13
00:00:54.819 --> 00:00:55.839
Peter was also there.

14
00:00:55.859 --> 00:01:01.437
"Now, Mother," said Peter, "tell us about the Russian gentleman.

15
00:01:02.557 --> 00:01:03.577
We have been patient.

16
00:01:04.678 --> 00:01:06.778
Make a nice long story of it."

17
00:01:06.798 --> 00:01:11.279
"I can't make a long story of it tonight," said Mother.

18
00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:13.680
"I'm very tired."

19
00:01:15.461 --> 00:01:18.261
Bobbie could tell from Mother's voice that Mother had been crying.

20
00:01:19.282 --> 00:01:20.342
But the others didn't know.

21
00:01:20.362 --> 00:01:27.004
"Well, make it as long as you can," said Phyllis, and Bobbie snuggled up to Mother.

22
00:01:29.832 --> 00:01:31.312
"Well," began Mother.

23
00:01:31.332 --> 00:01:33.553
"This man, Mr.

24
00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:36.514
Schepansky, wrote a book about how to help poor people.

25
00:01:37.494 --> 00:01:41.515
In Russia, criticizing wealthy people is against the rules of the czar.

26
00:01:42.556 --> 00:01:42.956
So Mr.

27
00:01:42.996 --> 00:01:46.317
Schepansky was sent to prison for three years in Siberia."

28
00:01:46.337 --> 00:01:51.358
"But Mother, that can't be true," cried Peter.

29
00:01:51.378 --> 00:01:55.119
"It is true, my dears," Mother said.

30
00:01:55.139 --> 00:01:58.480
"He was sent to prison because of his ideas.

31
00:01:59.508 --> 00:02:01.089
He had not done any crime.

32
00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:04.932
The prisoners work in the mines in the cold winters.

33
00:02:06.093 --> 00:02:08.595
If someone is sick, they are left to die."

34
00:02:08.615 --> 00:02:12.237
"How did he get away?"

35
00:02:12.657 --> 00:02:13.338
asked Phyllis.

36
00:02:13.358 --> 00:02:16.140
"He escaped," Mother said.

37
00:02:17.241 --> 00:02:20.183
"His wife and children left Russia and came to England.

38
00:02:21.123 --> 00:02:22.605
But he doesn't know where they are.

39
00:02:23.705 --> 00:02:27.128
When he finds his family, maybe they can live together here."

40
00:02:30.784 --> 00:02:34.826
Then Mother looked sad and said, "Let's say a prayer for all prisoners."

41
00:02:36.087 --> 00:02:37.708
They did that and went to bed.

42
00:02:38.668 --> 00:02:40.249
But Bobbie stayed up for a while.

43
00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:43.391
She had decided to write a letter to the old gentleman.

44
00:02:44.351 --> 00:02:51.495
She asked him to meet her the next morning: My dearest Old Gentleman, I really want to ask

45
00:02:51.535 --> 00:02:52.076
you something.

46
00:02:52.996 --> 00:02:54.817
I do not want you to give me anything.

47
00:02:55.818 --> 00:02:56.998
Mother says that is wrong.

48
00:02:57.999 --> 00:03:00.040
I only want to talk with you about a prisoner.

49
00:03:01.216 --> 00:03:03.197
Please get off the train tomorrow so we can talk.

50
00:03:04.178 --> 00:03:12.003
Your little friend, Bobbie The next morning Bobbie was waiting when the old gentleman got off the train.

51
00:03:12.023 --> 00:03:16.967
"Well," said the old gentleman, tapping Bobbie's shoulder, "what is it?"

52
00:03:16.987 --> 00:03:19.288
"Oh! You came!"

53
00:03:19.689 --> 00:03:21.230
replied Bobbie, turning round.

54
00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:25.152
"Well And she told him the story of the Russian.

55
00:03:25.172 --> 00:03:28.354
"Oh!" the old gentleman exclaimed.

56
00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:30.596
"I've read his book.

57
00:03:31.484 --> 00:03:33.965
It's translated into every European language.

58
00:03:35.146 --> 00:03:36.126
It's a noble book.

59
00:03:37.226 --> 00:03:38.587
I'll do my best to help him."

60
00:03:38.607 --> 00:03:41.008
"I was sure you could help!"

61
00:03:41.328 --> 00:03:42.448
said Bobbie excitedly.

62
00:03:42.468 --> 00:03:43.889
"Thank you."

63
00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:50.192
Ten days later the three children sat on the hill watching the 5:15 steam past.

64
00:03:51.972 --> 00:03:55.334
When they saw the old gentleman get off the train, they ran to meet him.

65
00:03:55.354 --> 00:03:57.194
"Good news!"

66
00:03:57.635 --> 00:03:58.075
he said.

67
00:03:58.095 --> 00:04:00.996
"I've found the Russian writer's family!

68
00:04:02.544 --> 00:04:03.565
You run and tell him."

69
00:04:04.866 --> 00:04:08.108
Bobbie ran home ahead and told the news to Mother and the Russian.

70
00:04:08.948 --> 00:04:10.769
The Russian man cried with happiness.

71
00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:15.252
That day he left for London and was reunited with his wife and children.
